cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RepoGen in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "RepoGen: genomic-driven drug repurposing from GWAS summary statistics"
abstract: >-
  RepoGen identifies drug repurposing candidates from GWAS summary statistics
  by combining three independent lines of evidence: MAGMA-based drug-target and
  ATC-class enrichment, reversal of imputed disease expression signatures using
  S-PrediXcan and LINCS L1000, and cis-eQTL Mendelian randomisation with
  colocalisation. Results from the three branches are reported separately and
  at their intersection.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/IvanAndru/RepoGen"
authors:
  - family-names: Andrushevich Petukhov
    given-names: Ivan
    affiliation: King's College London
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3161-607X"
keywords:
  - drug repurposing
  - GWAS
  - Mendelian randomisation
  - transcriptomics
  - bioinformatics
  - psychiatric genetics
